SysUpdater Debian packaging
===========================

The Debian source package must be built from a clean upstream source tree.

Generated CMake output, compiled binaries, object files, and the historical
packaging/opt_structure staging tree are not upstream source and must not be
included in the orig tarball.

The Debian package uses the normal filesystem hierarchy:
- executables: /usr/bin
- static application data: /usr/share/sysupdater
- desktop files: /usr/share/applications
- icon: /usr/share/pixmaps/sysupdater.png

Per-user mutable state is not installed below /usr. SysUpdater stores its
package hold-state under the user's XDG configuration directory.
Administrator passwords are never persisted to disk.
